bbox":[0,672,1405,158]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-2","number":"1B","markdown":"Solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y^4+2y}{4x-xy^3-2y^4}.\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-2-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,822,1405,108]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-3","number":"1C","markdown":"From the data given below, compute \n\n$$\n\\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right)_{x=3}\n$$\n\n and \n\n$$\n\\left(\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right)_{x=-2}\n$$\n\n.\n\n| $x$ | -2 | -1 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| $y$ | 0 | 1 | 6 | 24 | 60 | 120 |","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-3-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,922,1405,208],"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-3-diagram-1","caption":"Printed data table for x and y values (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-3-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,922,1405,208]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-4","number":"2A","markdown":"Using Runge Kutta method of fourth order, solve $y' = x + y^2$ with $y(0)=1$ at $x=0.2$ in steps of length $h=0.1$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-4-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1121,1405,105]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-5","number":"2B","markdown":"Solve \n\n$$\n(3y^4+3x^2y^2)\\,dx + (x^3y-3xy^3)\\,dy = 0.\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-5-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1218,1405,77]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-6","number":"2C","markdown":"Find the approximate value of \n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\sqrt{\\cos\\theta}\\,d\\theta\n$$\n\n using Simpson’s 1/3rd rule by dividing $\\left[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right]$ into 6 equal parts.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-6-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1287,1405,153]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-7","number":"3A","markdown":"Using Gauss Seidel method solve the system of equations\n\n$$\n10x_1 - 2x_2 - x_3 - x_4 = 3\n$$\n\n$$\n-2x_1 + 10x_2 - x_3 - x_4 = 15\n$$\n\n$$\n-x_1 - x_2 + 10x_3 - 2x_4 = 27\n$$\n\n$$\n-x_1 - x_2 - 2x_3 + 10x_4 = -9\n$$\n\nTake the initial approximation as $x_2=x_3=x_4=0$.\nCarry out 3 iterations and correct up to 4 decimal places.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-7-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1432,1405,296]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-8","number":"3B","markdown":"Solve the differential equation \n\n$$\n(D^2+1)y = \\sec x \\tan x\n$$\n\n by the method of variation of parameters.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-8-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1720,1405,160]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-9","number":"3C","markdown":"Compute a real root of \n\n$$\n3x-\\cos x-1=0\n$$\n\n using the Newton-Raphson method with $x_0=0.6$ correct to four decimal places.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-9-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,94,1405,108]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-10","number":"4A","markdown":"Using Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process, construct an orthonormal set of vectors from the set $\\{(1,2,1),(1,0,1),(3,1,0)\\}$ for $\\mathbb{R}^3$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-10-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,194,1405,122]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-11","number":"4B","markdown":"Solve \n\n$$\n(2x+3)^2\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}-(2x+3)\\frac{dy}{dx}-12y=6x.\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-11-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,308,1405,88]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-12","number":"4C","markdown":"Find the eigen values and one of the eigen vectors of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -6 & 2\\\\ -6 & 7 & -4\\\\ 2 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-12-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,388,1405,148],"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-12-diagram-1","caption":"Printed 3x3 matrix A (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-12-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,388,1405,148]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-13","number":"5A","markdown":"Define minimal spanning set of vectors. Prove that a minimal spanning set of vectors forms a basis for a vector space $V$ over $F$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-13-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,528,1405,96]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-14","number":"5B","markdown":"Given \n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=1+x y\n$$\n\n with the initial condition $y(0)=1$. Using Taylor series method, compute $y(0.1)$ correct to four decimal places by considering terms up to fourth order.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-14-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,616,1405,132]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-15","number":"5C","markdown":"Using the Gauss-Jordan method, find the inverse of:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1\\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-15-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,740,1405,1140],"id":"0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91-q-15-diagram-1","caption":"Printed 3x3 matrix A for inverse by Gauss-Jordan method (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/0dc403d3c9f8cb920c91/q-15-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,740,1405,1140]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]}],"warnings":["Transcribed from original page images with gpt-5.4-mini. Automatic transcription is not independent human verification."]}
